cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this testbed, its rule set, or its reported results, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Compliance-by-Design Simulation Testbed for City Digital Twins Under China's Data-Security Standards"
abstract: >-
  A domain-agnostic simulation testbed that formalises Chinese data-security
  standards (GB/T 43697-2024, GB/T 39786-2021, GB/T 22239-2019, GB/T 45109.1-2024,
  20262810-T-907 draft, PIPL, SL/T 853-855-2025) as machine-checkable constraints
  R1-R8, and measures the effect of compliance-by-design on cross-organisational
  evidence handover in city digital twins. Ships an engine/ruleset/profiles
  separation with a flood-twin validation case and an urban-transport
  generalisation probe. Version 1.0.4 reproduces the scenario suite, the
  SL/T 853-855 phase stress contrast, and the Morris/Sobol sensitivity analysis,
  and ships the supplementary tables named in the accompanying manuscript's
  data-availability statement.
